Chapter: IntLiteralUnderscore
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A decimal literal with digit-grouping underscores whose character
 count exceeds nineteen but whose value fits in a 64-bit Integer must
 be accepted. The overflow checker skips grouping underscores and
 leading zeros before counting significant digits; earlier it compared
 the CCE text against ASCII codes for '0' and '_', so no underscore or
 leading zero was ever skipped and this literal was falsely rejected as
 an overflow.

Section: Definitions

  billion-squared : Integer = 1_000_000_000_000_000_000

  padded : Integer = 000_000_042

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("grouped: " & show billion-squared)
    print-line-uni ("padded: " & show padded)
  end

